      "rev_n_1_363863_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_363863_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_363863",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: BFS Approach with Direction Handling\n\nThe initial approach using BFS needs adjustments to correctly handle the movement constraints and ensure all possible paths are considered. Specifically, we need to account for the possibility of moving north, east, west, and potentially using the ocean's currents to move east or west temporarily. We should modify the BFS to explore these additional movements and update the DP table accordingly. Additionally, we need to ensure that the BFS explores all valid paths efficiently and correctly counts the number of distinct routes to the castle.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_363863_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_fcd6b13099",
        "created_at": 1794505029.73998
      },
      "rev_n_2_31f7cf_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_31f7cf_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_31f7cf",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Use Depth-First Search (DFS) with Backtracking to explore all possible paths recursively, keeping track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant calculations. This approach ensures that all distinct paths to the castle are explored and counted correctly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_31f7cf_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_baf137d100",
        "created_at": 1794505075.585624
      },
      "rev_n_3_00ed29_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_00ed29_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_00ed29",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1 (revised): Ensure correct handling of the initial position and path counting logic. Specifically, check if the starting position contains the castle and handle the base case properly in the DFS function.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_00ed29_0",
