        "node_id": "n_4_680169",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-2: Ensure proper handling of both explicit sail movements and current-driven movements in the BFS traversal. Specifically, after processing the current cell's explicit sail movements, also consider the effect of the ocean's currents on the next cell's state before adding it to the queue. This ensures that all potential paths, including those influenced by currents, are explored and counted accurately.",
