        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-3: Dynamic Programming with Memoization\n\nTo address the issue, we need to refine our dynamic programming approach to correctly handle the movement constraints and ensure all possible paths are considered. Specifically, we should:\n\n1. Use memoization to store intermediate results and avoid redundant calculations.\n2. Ensure that the BFS explores all valid paths efficiently and correctly counts the number of distinct routes to the castle.\n3. Handle the special cases where the ship can use the ocean's currents to move east or west temporarily.\n\nBy implementing these improvements, we can accurately determine the number of distinct paths the ship can take to reach the castle.",
