        "thought_text": "Thought-3: Recursive Backtracking with Memoization\n\nTo solve this problem, we can use recursive backtracking with memoization. This approach allows us to explore all possible paths from the current position to the castle while keeping track of the number of distinct routes. By using memoization, we avoid redundant calculations and improve efficiency. We will define a recursive function that tries moving in all possible directions (north, east, west, and using the ocean's currents) and uses a dictionary to store the results of subproblems to prevent recomputation. This ensures that we count all distinct paths to the castle accurately.",
